<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply kept steady in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply kept steady in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said it left money market liquidity little changed in the week to June 30 despite a seasonal rise in notes in circulation</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   447.800 ( + 0.286)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  21.657 ( + 4.358)  Commercial bills			  2.361 ( + 0.050)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   25.794 ( + 0.000)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 114.712 ( - 5.177)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   482.465 ( + 3.767)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
